---
const faqs = [
  {
    question:
      "Does LKProfessionals only work with the industries listed here?",
    answer:
      "No. These pages represent sectors where our broader technology capabilities can be applied clearly. We can assess requirements from other industries where the project fits our technical and delivery capabilities.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do you use the same solution for every industry?",
    answer:
      "No. Reusable engineering patterns can improve efficiency, but workflows, permissions, integrations, terminology and user journeys should be shaped around the organisation and its operating requirements.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can one project combine several LKProfessionals services?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Many practical projects combine web or software development with integrations, automation, analytics, infrastructure, cybersecurity or ongoing support.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can you work with systems an organisation already uses?",
    answer:
      "Potentially. Existing systems can be retained or integrated where they remain useful and suitable technical interfaces, permissions and project conditions are available.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Do industry pages mean every organisation needs custom software?",
    answer:
      "No. Custom development should be used where it creates enough operational value. In some cases a website, integration, configuration change or smaller automation project is the better solution.",
  },
  {
    question:
      "Can LKProfessionals support organisations outside Sri Lanka?",
    answer:
      "Yes. Projects can be delivered remotely for international organisations, subject to the requirements, communication model, contractual arrangements and any project-specific constraints.",
  },
];
---

<section class="industries-faq">
  <div class="site-container industries-faq__layout">
    <div>
      <p>Industries FAQ</p>

      <h2>
        Industry knowledge without one-size-fits-all thinking.
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="industries-faq__list">
      {
        faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details>
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .industries-faq {
    padding-block: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 9rem);
    background: #f6f8fb;
  }

  .industries-faq__layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
      minmax(17rem, 0.7fr)
      minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem);
  }

  .industries-faq__layout
    > div:first-child > p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: #0b2f8f;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .industries-faq h2 {
    max-width: 12ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: #0d203c;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4.6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.05em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .industries-faq__list {
    border-top: 1px solid #dce3ec;
  }

  .industries-faq details {
    border-bottom: 1px solid #dce3ec;
    padding-block: 1rem;
  }

  .industries-faq summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    color: #293b53;
    font-size: 0.76rem;
    font-weight: 740;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .industries-faq details p {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0 0;
    color: #788497;
    font-size: 0.69rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  @media (max-width: 52rem) {
    .industries-faq__layout {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
